From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_DRAIN_TO_POOL=2: one line per pressure drain with the allocator's device memory before and after (what went back to the driver), the room left inside the blocks by kind, the pool's largest free piece before and after, and the deleted buffers that waited by size; count only, off by default

Switches: EDEN_UP_DRAIN_TO_POOL=2 (exact; the line only) or =1 (the line and 0896's own memory).
Acts with EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN=1 or 2 (the line is written by RasterizerVulkan::PressureDrainLook
after each drain). Line (stderr), the first 32 drains and every 16th:
"EDEN_UP_DRAIN_TO_POOL drain <n>: <freed> MiB freed, <back> MiB of it back to the driver (device
memory <before> -> <after> MiB, objects <a> -> <b>); room left inside the blocks <slack> MiB
(buffer pool <s> of <blocks> MiB blocks, sparse/trim pools <s>, default blocks <s>); largest free
piece <before> -> <after> MiB; deleted buffers that waited by size: under 1 MiB <x>, 1 MiB to half
a pool block <y>, larger <z> MiB; memory of their own since the last line: <n> buffers <m> MiB,
<r> went to the pool after all".

Why: after the 13 Nov drains (run1395, run1397: 934-1,268 MiB freed) the census showed 720-782 MiB
empty inside the allocator's blocks and only about 50-340 MiB came back to the pool; the existing
line has only the allocator's use (allocationBytes) and the largest free piece at the look, BEFORE
the drain (vk_rasterizer.cpp 3188, printed at 3305: the 239 and 8 MiB in those lines are before,
not after). Nothing says which blocks keep the freed room or how big the drained buffers were.

What: MemoryAllocator::DeviceMemory (vmaGetHeapBudgets: blockBytes and blockCount, which count
VMA's blocks and its allocations of their own alike, vk_mem_alloc.h 3.3.0 AllocateVulkanMemory)
before and after the drain, under the drain's own lock; the three separate pools' statistics
(Device::AddSeparatePoolUsage) after it; a walk of the deleted buffers before it
(BufferCache::ForEachDeleted, the same ring DeletedWaiting walks) split at 1 MiB and at half a
separate-pool block (Device::SeparatePoolBlockSize()/2: 8 MiB; larger ones take memory of their
own by VMA's rule); the pool's largest free piece again after it.
Off: one test of a static per drain.

Translation id: vk_rasterizer.cpp, pressure_drain.h, drain_to_pool.h (new),
vulkan_memory_allocator.{h,cpp} and buffer_cache_base.h are not in gen-translation-id.py's inputs
(none is a hashed single file, none is reached from src/shader_recompiler: checked against
t166c/translation_inputs-7f97.txt, 418 files), and EDEN_UP_DRAIN_TO_POOL is not in
TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

